.TH "zilc" "1" "2026\-10\-30"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
zilc \- Intermediate representation lowerer (ZIL to QBE SSA)
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBzilc\fR [\fIoptions\fR] <input.\&zil> [\fIoutput.\&ssa\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBzilc\fR lowers Zoril Intermediate Language (ZIL) into QBE Static Single Assignment (SSA) intermediate representation.\& It forms the second stage of the Zoril compilation pipeline, bridging the compiler frontend (\fBzoril\fR(1)) and the machine code backend (\fBqbe\fR(1)).\&
.PP
The output goes to \fIoutput.\&ssa\fR, or to the file named by \fB\-o\fR; with neither, \fBzilc\fR writes it to standard output.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR <file>
.RS 4
Write lowered QBE SSA output to <file>.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-module\fR <name>
.RS 4
Override the target module name used during SSA generation.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display usage instructions and command\-line options, then exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display version information and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Lower a program \fBzoril\fR(1) wrote, or one written by hand, and build it with the host tools:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
zilc prog\&.zil prog\&.ssa
qbe \-o prog\&.s prog\&.ssa
as \-o prog\&.o prog\&.s
ld \-o prog /usr/local/lib/zoril/runtime\&.o prog\&.o
.fi
.RE
.PP
With no output file the SSA goes to standard output:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
zilc prog\&.zil | qbe | as \-o prog\&.o
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBzilc\fR checks types; the ownership and region checks run in \fBzoril\fR(1) before it writes ZIL, so hand\-written ZIL carries none of them.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Compilation and lowering succeeded.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB>0\fR
.RS 4
An error occurred during parsing, validation, or SSA lowering.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBzoril\fR(1), \fBzbuild\fR(1)
